+# Cluster ci-1755c410599471fe — RowTableViewTest uses the Qt 6-only `itemDelegateForIndex`
+
+**Decision: REAL (test-side build regression), fixed.** The hosted `linux-arm64` Qt 5 build of the pinned commit
+`31f559ab479dcd1b822545aae477222f58f32c0d` stops at `tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:54` and `:57` because
+`QAbstractItemView::itemDelegateForIndex` does not exist in Qt 5. The product class is not involved: `RowTableView`
+inherits `QTableView`, and the two test queries are the only uses of that spelling in the tree. The test now selects
+the API by Qt version and keeps the same assertion.
+
+## Evidence
+
+- Hosted CI log
+  `/home/kruzzzzy/.local/share/zene-bunny-fix/qwen/train-ci/31f559ab479dcd1b822545aae477222f58f32c0d/run-43764792400-job-132967358689.log:6725`
+  and `:6732`:
+  `error: 'class lmms::gui::RowTableView' has no member named 'itemDelegateForIndex'; did you mean 'itemDelegateForRow'?`
+  at `tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:54` and `:57`, followed by the `gmake` failure of
+  `tests/CMakeFiles/RowTableViewTest.dir`.
+- HEAD is the pinned commit: `git log -1 --oneline` = `31f559ab47 Revert "Merge feat/050-Q050-481.4-oc ..."`.
+- Qt 5.15.19 header `/usr/include/qt/QtWidgets/qabstractitemview.h:226` declares
+  `itemDelegate(const QModelIndex &index) const`; it has no `itemDelegateForIndex`. Qt 6 header
+  `/usr/include/qt6/QtWidgets/qabstractitemview.h:204-208` deprecates `itemDelegate(index)` in favour of the virtual
+  `itemDelegateForIndex(index)`, so replacing the call unconditionally with the Qt 5 spelling would break a
+  `-Werror` Qt 6 build.
+- `grep -rn itemDelegateForIndex --exclude-dir=build .` before the fix found exactly the two test uses at `:54` and
+  `:57`; there is no product use and no other caller to keep consistent.
+- The local configured build tree is Qt 6; the local Qt 5.15.19 toolchain (`moc` 5.15.19, `qmake` using Qt 5.15.19
+  in `/usr/lib`) is used to reproduce the hosted Qt 5 failure directly.
+
+## Fix
+
+`tests/src/gui/RowTableViewTest.cpp:32-40` adds one local helper:
+
+```cpp
+// QAbstractItemView::itemDelegateForIndex is Qt 6; Qt 5's spelling is itemDelegate(index).
+static const QAbstractItemDelegate* rowDelegate(const RowTableView& view, const QModelIndex& index)
+{
+#if QT_VERSION >= QT_VERSION_CHECK(6, 0, 0)
+	return view.itemDelegateForIndex(index);
+#else
+	return view.itemDelegate(index);
+#endif
+}
+```
+
+Both call sites (`:64`, `:67`) use it. The assertion is unchanged: the delegate on the inserted row is compared with
+the delegate on the pre-existing row. This is a test-only portability fix; no product code, command, save format,
+undo step or audio-thread path is touched.
+
